# S5-07 automatic within-series comparison, 2026-11-15

Purpose: verify that one `linux-direct --test-runs 2` invocation persists the
series evidence, automatically writes `comparison.json`, and uses the strict
comparator for the new Stage 4 init-nonce run pair.

## Invocation and inputs

- Worktree: `codex`; runner source revision
  `280494280761e8754dabd5917b3ab1a5a3148e69`, `source_dirty=false`.
- Host: macOS/aarch64; `od-runner` 0.1.0, release build.
- Kernel SHA-256:
  `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256:
  `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256:
  `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`;
  expected ACPI manifest hash:
  `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2`.
- Scenario `stage4-init-nonce`, `smoke_not_acceptance`, counted `stage4a`
  (`--set-cpl0 --user-mode`), 128 MiB RAM, budget 3,000,000,000,
  expected stop `budget_exhausted`.
- Full command:

  ```sh
  target/release/od-runner linux-direct --test-runs 2 --series-id stage5-s5-07-stage4a-auto-compare-20261115-a --scenario-id stage4-init-nonce --expected-stop-kind budget_exhausted --out work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-stage4a-auto-compare-20261115-a/series.json --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic --initramfs /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e --expected-initramfs-sha256 ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588 --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode
  ```

## Outcome

The command produced `series.json`, two run directories, and the new
`comparison.json` in one invocation. The aggregate scenario outcome was
`passed`; both runs started the guest, emitted their exact nonce, stopped at
`budget_exhausted`, and retired 2,999,999,998 instructions.

| Run | Nonce | Exceptions | IRQ0 edges | Delivered IRQs | Quanta | Wall seconds | UART bytes |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | `OD518e825e3105f3ec0000062ed00000000` | 34 PF + 1 GP | 34,781 | 34,786 | 34,547,130 | 1116.432 | 24,209 |
| 0002 | `OD518e826e703c80660000062ed00000001` | 34 PF + 1 GP | 34,816 | 34,821 | 34,581,135 | 1113.875 | 23,441 |

The runner printed:

```text
within-series comparison: matches=false explained=1 unexplained=2 path=work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-stage4a-auto-compare-20261115-a/comparison.json
unexplained differences: ["run[1].machine_observations differs", "run[1].ordered_uart_bytes differs after nonce normalization"]
```

Both scenario runs passed, but the series comparison did not. The production
exit mapping returns exit 1 when a passed scenario has an unmatched strict
comparison. The session output did not retain the numeric process exit code
separately. This does **not** meet S5-07 repeatability acceptance.

## Difference analysis

The machine observations include IRQ/quantum variation despite matching
exception counts: IRQ0 edges are 34,781/34,816, delivered IRQs 34,786/34,821,
and refused-masked IRQs 1,509,240/954,250. The terminal panic traces also
differ. Run 0001 contains optional frames including
`update_cfs_rq_load_avg`, `update_load_avg`, `update_curr`, `dequeue_entity`,
`psi_group_change`, `psi_task_switch`, and `schedule`; run 0002 contains
`handle_mm_fault`. The Stage 4 terminal-snapshot normalizer does not allow all
of these observed optional frames, so the specialized volatile-observation
comparison is not eligible for this pair. This explains why the comparator
kept the differences strict; it does not establish that the underlying IRQ or
stack variation is benign. No allowlist or comparison rule was changed for
this run.

S5-07 remains blocked/unaccepted. Preserve this passing-but-unrepeatable pair
as evidence; do not overwrite the prior failed common-ID series.

